itations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1096143A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INO KAZUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI YOSHINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INO, KAZUYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOU, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, YOSHINORI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INO KAZUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATOU HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI YOSHINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INO, KAZUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOU, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, YOSHINORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hydraulic motor capable of minimizing a wear caused on a rotating brake disk of a brake device, wherein a rotating brake disk (32) which forms a plurality of arc-shaped grooves (17) apart from each other in circumferential direction and constitutes a brake device (31) is provided on the outer peripheral side of a cylinder block (15), and a plurality of arc-shaped projections (33) engaged with the arc-shaped grooves (17) and a plurality of radial contact parts (34) are provided on the inner peripheral side of the rotating brake disk (32) and the plurality of radial contact parts (34) are allowed to face the outer peripheral surface of the cylinder block (15) so that they can be brought into contact with each other, whereby, at the time of braking of the hydraulic motor (10), the movement of the rotating brake disk (32) in rotating direction is controlled by the arc-shaped projections (33) and the movement of the rotating brake disk (32) in radial direction is controlled by the radial contact parts (34).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un moteur hydraulique capable de réduire l'usure d'un disque de frein rotatif d'un dispositif de frein. La face périphérique externe du bloc-cylindres (15) est pourvue d'un disque de frein rotatif (32) formant une pluralité de rainures en arc (17) disjointes, circulairement distribuées, et constituant un dispositif de frein (31). La face périphérique interne du disque de frein rotatif (32) est pourvue, d'une part d'une pluralité de protubérances en arc (33) venant au contact des rainures en arc (17), et d'autre part de pièces de contact radiales (34) orientées vers la face périphérique externe du bloc-cylindres (15) de façon à pouvoir être amenées au contact les unes des autres. Pour freiner le moteur hydraulique (10), le principe est de commander le mouvement du disque de frein rotatif (32), d'une part dans le sens de rotation au moyen des protubérances en arc (33), et d'autre part radialement au moyen des pièces de contact radiales (34).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>